# Government AI Grants for Business (Canada & Ontario)

## 1. Federal & Cross-Canada AI Grants
* **NRC IRAP & AI Assist:** Covers 50%–80% of technical staff/contractor salaries for building custom AI models or experimental R&D.
* **AI Compute Access Fund:** $100,000 to $5,000,000 (50%–66% coverage) for GPU, cloud, and high-performance hardware costs.
* **Scale AI (Supercluster):** Co-funds up to 50% of project costs for applying AI to supply chain, logistics, and workflow automation.
* **SR&ED Tax Credit:** 35%–69% back on technical labor and R&D expenses for developing proprietary algorithms.

## 2. Ontario Provincial AI Grants
* **DCC — Tech Demonstration (OCI):** Up to $50,000 (50% matched) to adopt/install AI tools, voice AI, automations, and software.
* **DCC — Digital Modernization (OCI):** Up to $15,000 (50% matched) for strategy, architecture design, and roadmaps before deployment.
* **Critical Industrial Technologies (CIT):** Up to $200,000 (50% coverage) for SMEs deploying AI/robotics in manufacturing, agri-food, or mining.
* **Collaborate 2 Commercialize (C2C):** Up to $150,000+ for commercializing IP in partnership with university/college AI labs.
* **Ontario Innovation Tax Credit (OITC):** 8% refundable tax credit stacking on top of federal SR&ED (gives up to 43% cash back on Ontario dev labor).
* **Canada-Ontario Job Grant (COJG):** Up to $10,000–$15,000 per employee (50%–83% covered) to train staff on using AI productivity platforms.

## 3. Stacking Strategy & Key Rules
* **Building Custom Tech:** Stacking IRAP + SR&ED + OITC offsets up to 75%–80% of developer salaries.
* **Adopting AI Tools:** Use OCI DCC Tech Demonstration or COJG training grants.
* **Approval Tip:** Frame projects around technical risk and uncertainty rather than simple off-the-shelf software integration.